{"record_type": "item", "id": "dd20e9deb82a4be387d57ba709597bfb", "response_id": "turn_4968bcd8625944179bfe7c9c1de5c49e", "type": "message", "status": "completed", "created_at": 1791082966, "role": "user", "content": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "The three-planet fit F8 (2.220, 3.797, 5.684 d) was submitted and failed on planet count, so the true count is 2 or 4. Using the residuals of F1 (one planet at 2.219 d), F4 (2.22+3.79 d) and F5 (2.22+5.65 d): which of the secondary signals (3.79 d, 5.65 d, 14.2 d, 6.9 d) is most credible as a planet, and are any likely stellar-rotation harmonics or aliases of each other (e.g., 3.79 and 5.65 as P_rot/3 and P_rot/2 of a ~11-12 d rotation, or as aliases of one another)? Recommend which two-planet configuration (if any) is best supported. Be quick; record an evidence note."}]}
